A||||5||Formula 18||ORGE (or others), I need your help!||||1||
Z||000000||Formula 18||11-15-2000||08:57 PM||||Will a turbo chip has been programmed for the 87/88 Fieros with Automatic transmissions with stock injectors, MAP sensor, injectors ect... work on a 88 with a 5 speed?? <P>What diffreances in drivabilty will I see? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tom88gt||11-15-2000||09:13 PM||||I would guess no.  I think the chip makers offer different ones for each engine/trans combination.  Also, I've heard mixed reviews as to the effectiveness of these aftermarket chips.  Apparantly Delco did their homework.  That said, if someone has documented proof, before and after dyno results with nothing changed but the chips, then I would be tempted to buy one as well.  Many owners add chips and think its more powerful without proof, but there is a strong psycological reason for that.<P>Basicially, your a guinnee pig.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula 18||11-16-2000||02:44 PM||||The reason I was going to switch chips was because this one has reprogramed fuel pules too spray more fuel when the car is under boost.  I am going to be running a turbo. <BR>I don't want to spen the $$ to find out that it won't work with a 5-speed ||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||11-16-2000||08:26 PM||||Well.... the obvious dif between an auto and a stick chip is the programming of the line that controls the shift light or the TCC on the ECM. (The same ECM terminal is used for both functions.) <P>It would run but I wouldn't count on the thing working right. There's also some other transmission specific programming issues that aren't obvious as well as fuel & ignition tuning parameters that are diferant.||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||11-18-2000||12:17 AM||||It will work, but you will be missings a few little things like shift anticipation (float the RPM during shifts), no shift light (wires not even there on automatic cars). Otherwise, it will work and run, but it might stall on a throttle snap close. <P>Does the current chip use a 2 bar map? ESC module? Boost control?<P>Email me off line. I can possibly help.<P>Terry<BR> <p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 11-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||11-18-2000||12:45 PM||||The ECM terminal that runs the shift light in a stick car runs the the TC lock in an automatic. When an auto chip is used on a stick likely the shift light will come on when the ECM wants to lock the TC in the automatic. So far all the GM ECM's I've looked at work this way.||||reg||1
